Stub async imports the componentizer does not provide while snapshotting.

Wizer instantiates the component after wasmtime's
define_unknown_imports_as_traps, which stubs every function with func_new. An
`async func` import accepts only a concurrent host function, so a world that
imports an async function of the embedding host (Pane's
pane:extension/operations `call`) could not be componentized. This redefines
those interfaces with func_new_concurrent traps; nothing calls them during the
snapshot. Wasmtime 49 does this in define_unknown_imports_as_traps itself, so
moving componentize-qjs to it would retire this patch.

The componentizer defines the WASI 0.3 interfaces of wasmtime-wasi, which
leave out `wasi:http`, so its client (an async `send`, Pane's web requests)
is stubbed the same way.

Modifies componentize-qjs (Apache-2.0, see LICENSE-componentize-qjs); this
patch is distributed under the same license.

